    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="0498" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11597: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-13T13:00:00+08:00">December 13, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—1:28 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1140. Japanese Consulate General informs me that orders have been issued by
                    Japanese military and naval authorities to stop operations against Hohsien,
                    Anhui. Similar instructions are being conveyed to the Hohsien front by special
                    Japanese plane.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d626-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d626-f1" n="56" xml:id="d626-f1-content">
                <p>Colonel Hashimoto at Wuhu similarly assured British representatives that “Hohsien
                    would not be attacked until refugees had been evacuated.” (793.94/11615)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
